  "question": {
    "text": "A car of mass ' $m$ ' moves on a banked road having radius ' $r$ ' and banking angle $\\theta$. To avoid slipping from banked road, the maximum permissible speed of the car is $v_0$. The coefficient of friction $\\mu$ between the wheels of the car and the banked road is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "nwt69",
      "text": "$\\mu=\\frac{\\mathrm{v}_{\\mathrm{o}}^2+\\mathrm{rg} \\tan \\theta}{\\mathrm{rg}+\\mathrm{v}_{\\mathrm{o}}^2 \\tan \\theta}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "byapd",
      "text": "$\\mu=\\frac{v_0^2-r g \\tan \\theta}{r g-v_0^2 \\tan \\theta}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "CTpmt",
      "text": "$\\mu=\\frac{v_0^2-r g \\tan \\theta}{r g+v_0^2 \\tan \\theta}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ftrci",
      "text": "$\\mu=\\frac{v_o^2+r g \\tan \\theta}{\\mathrm{rg}-\\mathrm{v}_{\\mathrm{o}}^2 \\tan \\theta}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/H0D_W8zBZE6QUzYkJ7JmTebfsrJwleY7i9iANRAXpDw.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\nSo, $N=m g \\cos \\theta+\\frac{m v_0^2}{r} \\sin \\theta$\n$f_r=\\mu m g \\cos \\theta+\\frac{\\mu m v_0^2}{r} \\sin \\theta$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\text { And } \\frac{m v_0^2}{r} \\cos \\theta=m g \\sin \\theta+f_r \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\frac{m v_0^2}{r} \\cos \\theta-m g \\sin \\theta=\\mu\\left(m g \\cos \\theta+\\frac{m v_0^2}{r} \\sin \\theta\\right) \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow\\left(v_0^2-g r \\tan \\theta\\right)=\\mu\\left(v_0^2 \\tan \\theta+g r\\right) \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\mu=\\frac{v_0^2-g r \\tan \\theta}{g r+v_0^2 \\tan \\theta}\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
